{
  "_schema_version": 1,
  "slug": "right-sliding-drawer",
  "label": "Right sliding drawer",
  "description": "A non-modal quick view docked to the right edge, 550px wide, opened by clicking the body of a result card. The page behind it stays live and interactive: the selected card keeps its highlight and the filter rail keeps working. The header carries the item title, an optional primary action, and three icon buttons. The body scrolls independently and holds the item's summary, its pinned properties, and a tab bar whose panels are the same ones the full detail page shows.",
  "when": "Use when a user needs to inspect one item without losing the list they found it in, IN EXPLORER. Studio draws the same 550px shell with a different body, and it is captured separately as `studio-quick-edit-drawer`: that one edits the title in place and renders Properties as editable fields. The tab sets overlap rather than nest. Both carry Properties and Suggestions; only Studio carries General and People; only Explorer carries Description and Fields. Explorer shows five tabs and puts a result count on four of them, Studio shows four and counts none. The selector tells the two apart by `apps`, so this pointer is for a human reading one capture without reading the other. Do NOT use asset-detail-360: that is the full page this drawer previews, reached by clicking the item TITLE rather than the card body, and it carries tabs and sections the drawer omits. Do NOT use a modal for this: in the product a drawer and a modal are different surfaces, and the difference is not decorative. The drawer sets `::backdrop { display: none }` and is opened non-modally so the page stays usable behind it; the modal paints a 60% black backdrop and blocks the page. Reach for a modal when the user must answer before continuing, and for this drawer when they must not lose their place.",
  "apps": ["explorer"],
  "patterns": ["right-sliding-drawer"],
  "tags": [
    "drawer",
    "overlay",
    "quick-view",
    "detail",
    "panel",
    "non-modal",
    "preview"
  ],
  "derivedFrom": {
    "surface": "Explorer > Search > result card body > quick view",
    "capturedOn": "2026-09-30",
    "productVersion": "manufacturing.zeenea.app/explorer",
    "screenshot": "captures/right-sliding-drawer.png"
  },
  "reference": "product",
  "slots": {
    "header": "Item title and its technical name in brackets, a Request Access action, and three icon buttons: favourite, open in full page, close.",
    "tags": "Item type, catalog folder, connection, and a data quality indicator carrying a coloured traffic light.",
    "summary": "A Summary heading with an information icon, over the item's description",
    "featured-properties": "A Featured properties heading over pinned label and value pairs, laid out as a definition list",
    "tabs": "A tab bar whose labels carry result counts, over the selected tab's panel",
    "glossary": "A Glossary heading over the item's glossary links, each an initials badge and its name.",
    "related": "A line counting the items this one is related to, with a link to the schema at the right."
  },
  "renderNotes": [
    "Children of a VERTICAL frame must omit `sizing`. `sizing.horizontal:\"FILL\"` emits `flex:1`, which in a column container distributes height instead of hugging content. `faceted-browse` carried 20 of these against its own notes and `tests/app-context-recipes.test.js` now walks every skeleton for the case.",
    "This recipe composes the overlay surface ONLY, at its captured width of 550px. In the product the dialog is `position: fixed` with `inset: 70px 0 0 0`, so it docks to the right edge below the app header and runs to the bottom of the viewport. The page beneath is not part of this composition and stays interactive.",
    "Every value is the captured quick view's (the Customers dataset, found by searching \"customer\" in Explorer, manufacturing.zeenea.app, 2026-09-30).",
    "The three icon buttons are `button` Emphasis=Icon-only with `Icon` favorite, view-detail and close, the glyphs the DS drawer's own Explorer header draws. Request Access is drawn without its leading icon: the product's glyph (a hand over a key) is not one `button` can take.",
    "The Data Quality tag's traffic light is red on this item; it is drawn as read-only-tag Status-error, whose leading icon is the error glyph, not the product's dot.",
    "Explorer's tabs put a count after four of the five labels; `tabs` has no count badge, so the count is written into the label text.",
    "The Description panel is the tenant's rich text: a heading, a paragraph and a schema table (drawn with `table`, cut here after four rows). The paragraph is left out: it is the tenant's writing, not product copy, and it uses a word the product's terminology forbids (\"record\")."
  ],
